          "type": "turn",
          "question": "What is the difference between flu and a cold?",
          "answer": "The flu and a cold are both respiratory infections but have distinct differences. \n\nA cold begins gradually, often featuring nasal symptoms and a sore throat, and rarely leads to a high fever or severe illness in adults. On the other hand, the flu typically starts suddenly with symptoms like fever, muscle aches, and significant fatigue, progressing to respiratory symptoms.\n\nInfluenza is generally more severe than a common cold and can lead to more serious health issues. It is important to note that the symptoms and severity may vary between individuals. These distinctions can help guide discussions with a healthcare provider if needed.\n\nI could not cover any treatment options or specific management strategies beyond describing the conditions themselves.\n\nNot medical advice. This is an educational software project. It does not diagnose or treat, and it must not be used for real medical decisions.",
